add("T001","∀ (m : ℕ) (A : Set (GDVec m)) (s : ℝ), 0 < s → GDMeasure s A = MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure s A",[],["S001"],"Bridge the explicit countable-cover content supremum to hausdorffMeasure_apply. The nonempty-set supremum in GDCost handles empty sets exactly. Finite positive real scales are cofinal towards zero among positive ENNReal scales; the infinity scale cannot enlarge the supremum. No measurability of A or covering sets is required.");
add("T002",`∀ (m : ℕ) (A : Set (GDVec m)),
  (0 : ℝ≥0∞) ≤ dimH A ∧
  ∀ s : ℝ, 0 < s →
    GDMeasure s A = MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure s A ∧
    (ENNReal.ofReal s < dimH A → GDMeasure s A = ⊤) ∧
    (dimH A < ENNReal.ofReal s → GDMeasure s A = 0) ∧
    (GDMeasure s A < ⊤ → dimH A ≤ ENNReal.ofReal s) ∧
    (GDMeasure s A = 0 → dimH A ≤ ENNReal.ofReal s) ∧
    (GDMeasure s A = ⊤ → ENNReal.ofReal s ≤ dimH A)`,["T001"],["S002"],"Export the whole N001 normalization and critical-exponent package. Apply the pinned native dimension lemmas with d : NNReal equal to the positive exponent s, so its ENNReal coercion is ofReal s. The measure's real exponent is the NNReal-to-real coercion. The ambient Borel instances are canonical.");
add("T003",`Bornology.IsBounded E ∧ dimH E ≤ (n : ℝ≥0∞) ∧
  (n = 0 → E = Set.univ ∧ dimH E = 0)`,["H001","H002","T002"],["S003","S004","S005"],"Use compact boundedness, choose a containing coordinate box, and implement the supplied mesh-grid estimate when n>0. Costs tend to zero for each a>n and every target scale. In n=0, GDVec 0 is a singleton; nonemptiness gives E=univ and the one-set zero-cost covers give dimension zero. Keep the supplied grid and singleton proof route.");
add("T004",`Bornology.IsBounded E ∧
  (0 : ℝ≥0∞) ≤ dimH E ∧ dimH E ≤ (n : ℝ≥0∞) ∧ dimH E < ⊤ ∧
  (∀ s δ : ℝ, 0 < s → 0 < δ → GDContent s δ E < ⊤) ∧
  (n = 0 → E = Set.univ ∧ dimH E = 0)`,["H002","T003"],["S006"],"Export all N002 clauses. Finite covers by balls of radius δ/2 bound the content by a finite sum for every positive real s and δ. Dimension finiteness follows from the finite natural-number bound; no extra finiteness assumption is introduced.");
add("T005",`(∀ a : ℝ, 1 < a → GDMeasure a GDInterval = 0) ∧
  dimH GDInterval ≤ 1`,["T002"],["S007"],"Partition [0,1] into N equal intervals, use cost N^(1-a) tending to zero and mesh 1/N tending to zero, then N001 and the limit a↓1. GDInterval is a subset of ℝ, so applying N001 requires the one-coordinate Euclidean isometry; transport covers in both directions. This is a local coordinate identification, not a change of metric.");
add("T006",`∀ s δ : ℝ, 0 < s → s < 1 → 0 < δ →
  ENNReal.ofReal (δ ^ (s - 1)) ≤ GDContent s δ GDInterval`,[],["S008","S009"],"For arbitrary countable covers discard empty sets; bound the sum of diameters below by one using open interval enlargements and Lebesgue subadditivity. Then multiply by δ^(s-1), including the zero-diameter case, and take the content infimum. Here δ and exponent s-1 are real, so this power is Real.rpow; ofReal embeds its nonnegative value into ENNReal.");
add("T007",`dimH GDInterval = 1 ∧
  (∀ a : ℝ, 1 < a → GDMeasure a GDInterval = 0) ∧
  (∀ s δ : ℝ, 0 < s → s < 1 → 0 < δ →
    ENNReal.ofReal (δ ^ (s - 1)) ≤ GDContent s δ GDInterval) ∧
  (∀ s : ℝ, 0 < s → s < 1 → GDMeasure s GDInterval = ⊤)`,["T002","T005","T006"],["S010"],"Export every N003 clause. The lower-content bound diverges as δ↓0 for 0<s<1, giving infinite measure and dimension at least one, combined with T005. Use the same one-coordinate Euclidean identification when instantiating N001 on ℝ.");
add("T008",`1 ≤ n → ∀ q r ε : ℝ,
  dimH E < ENNReal.ofReal q → 0 < r → r ≤ 1 → 0 < ε →
  GDPositiveCover E q r ε`,["T002","T004"],["S011","S012","S013"],"Export N004. q>D implies q>0 even though q is an arbitrary real. Start with q-cost below ε/2 and replace zero-diameter singletons by positive-diameter balls with summable added cost, using n≥1; remove empty sets. K⊆ℕ is represented by the countable subtype K, with no nonemptiness or measurability premise on arbitrary ambient covering sets.");
add("T009",`(∀ (x y : GDVec n) (t u : ℝ),
    dist (GDPoint x t) (GDPoint y u) =
      Real.sqrt (dist x y ^ 2 + |t - u| ^ 2)) ∧
  (∀ z : GDVec (n + 1), ∃ (x : GDVec n) (t : ℝ), z = GDPoint x t)`,[],["S014","S016","S018","S026"],"Shared implementation of the stipulated coordinate identification. Fin.snoc appends the last coordinate; WithLp.toLp 2 places the tuple in the L2 norm. PiLp.dist_eq_of_L2 and the finite sum split give exactly the Euclidean product formula, including n=0. Splitting off the last coordinate gives surjectivity. No max-norm product distance is used or assumed.");
add("T010",`dimH (GDProduct E) ≤ dimH E + 1 ∧ dimH (GDProduct E) < ⊤`,["T002","T004","T007","T008","T009"],["S014","S015","S016","S017"],"Export N005. For n=0 transport interval covers along the coordinate isometry. For n≥1 use positive-diameter q-covers, r=min(1,δ/√2), partition I into ceil(1/r_i) intervals and apply T009 for the √2 diameter bound. The total (q+1)-cost is <2(√2)^(q+1)ε. Let ε↓0 at each scale, then q↓D. Use the established finiteness of D before interpreting its real value; retain the supplied cover construction.");
add("T011",`∀ s δ : ℝ, 0 < s → 0 < δ →
  ∀ (K : Set ℕ) (V : K → Set (GDVec (n + 1))),
    GDProduct E ⊆ ⋃ i, V i →
    (∀ i, (V i).Nonempty ∧ Metric.ediam (V i) ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ) →
    ∀ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε →
      GDContent s δ E ≤
        (∑' i, (Metric.ediam (V i)) ^ (s + 1)) + ENNReal.ofReal ε`,["T004","T009"],["S018","S019","S020","S021"],"The substantive slicing estimate for each arbitrary cover. Extract the first n and last coordinates; T009 gives their diameter bounds. Each diameter is finite, so use its real value ρ_i to set η_i=ε2^(-i-1)/(1+ρ_i^s) and enclose the last projection in an open interval J_i. The first projections selected by t∈J_i cover E. Integrate c≤Σρ_i^s 1_{J_i} against volume.restrict GDInterval. c is finite by N002, each indicator is Borel measurable, and the countable subtype K supports lintegral_tsum. Length(I)=1 and Ση_iρ_i^s≤ε give the stated ENNReal inequality. Covering sets themselves require no measurability.");
add("T012",`∀ s δ : ℝ, 0 < s → 0 < δ →
  GDContent s δ E ≤ GDContent (s + 1) δ (GDProduct E)`,["T011"],["S022"],"Export N006. Let ε↓0 in T011, treating an infinite cover-cost separately, then take the infimum over all countable δ-covers. Remove empty members without changing their GDCost, reindexing by K⊆ℕ; for s+1>0 GDCost equals the displayed diameter power on nonempty sets.");
add("T013",`∀ s : ℝ, 0 < s → ENNReal.ofReal s < dimH E →
  GDMeasure (s + 1) (GDProduct E) = ⊤`,["T002","T012"],["S023","S024"],"N001 gives infinite s-measure on E. For each finite bound choose a positive scale where its content exceeds that bound, transfer it with N006, and take the content supremum on F. This uses arbitrary finite bounds rather than a hidden limit-exchange assumption.");
add("T014",`0 < dimH E → dimH E + 1 ≤ dimH (GDProduct E)`,["T002","T004","T013"],["S025"],"Export N007. N001 converts infinite (s+1)-measure on F into a dimension bound for every 0<s<D. Use D<∞ from N002 and take s↑D. This includes all positive finite dimensions and introduces no restriction on n.");
add("T015",`dimH E = 0 → ∀ s δ : ℝ, 0 < s → 0 < δ →
  GDContent s δ GDInterval ≤ GDContent s δ (GDProduct E)`,["H001","T009"],["S026"],"Choose x0∈E. The slice t↦GDPoint x0 t is isometric by T009. Intersect any cover of F with its image and pull it back to obtain a cover of I with no larger diameters or s-cost; take infima. Keep the source branch assumption D=0, although the isometry construction itself uses only nonemptiness. No ambient max-product space is introduced.");
add("T016",`dimH E = 0 →
  (1 : ℝ≥0∞) ≤ dimH (GDProduct E) ∧
  (1 : ℝ≥0∞) = dimH E + 1`,["T002","T007","T015"],["S026","S027"],"Export N008. Supremize T015 over scales and use N003's infinite interval s-measure for 0<s<1. N001 gives dim_H F≥s; let s↑1 and substitute D=0. The coordinate construction remains valid for n=0.");
const conclusion="dimH (GDProduct E) = dimH E + 1";
add("T017",conclusion,["T004","T010","T014","T016"],["S028"],"Export P by cases D>0 or D=0, using N002's nonnegative finite dimension, N007/N008 for the lower bound, N005 for the upper bound and antisymmetry.");
const artifact={
header:load("header"),parameters,premise_types:{H001:"E.Nonempty",H002:"IsCompact E"},conclusion_type:conclusion,
representation:"Use GDVec m = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m) = PiLp 2 (fun _ : Fin m => ℝ), including m=0. The 2 is the ENNReal Lp exponent, not an index count: its metric is the square root of the sum of squared coordinate distances. GDPoint appends the real coordinate using Fin.snoc and WithLp.toLp 2; GDProduct E is exactly its image of E×[0,1] in GDVec (n+1). T009 checks the distance formula and decomposition. GDInterval is Icc (0:ℝ) 1. Metric.ediam is the ENNReal supremum of pairwise edist, with empty value zero and infinity for unbounded sets. GDCost uses an iSup over the proposition of set nonemptiness: this is zero for an empty set and otherwise the diameter's real power. GDContent takes iInf over sequences satisfying actual inclusion and scale bounds; GDMeasure takes iSup over positive real scales. Positive exponents have 0^s=0. ENNReal powers with real exponents resolve to ENNReal.rpow; the interval scale lower bound uses Real.rpow before ofReal. All costs and dimensions stay in ENNReal; ofReal s embeds a positive real exponent exactly, and natural n and numeral 1 are finite ENNReal values in dimension expressions. Native dimH is the iSup of nonnegative real exponents with infinite native Hausdorff measure under the Borel structure, with empty supremum zero. T001 proves the cover-to-native bridge; T002 uses inspected native lemmas with NNReal exponents. Boundedness is Bornology.IsBounded under the usual metric bornology. No M premise ports or background-note ports are needed; native Mathlib results are used directly. Lebesgue integration uses volume.restrict GDInterval and ENNReal-valued nonnegative integrals; lintegral_tsum requires Countable K and a.e. measurability, supplied by K⊆ℕ and open interval indicators, without measurability of arbitrary covers.",
objects:[],steps,terminal:"T017",
source_outputs:{N001:"T002",N002:"T004",N003:"T007",N004:"T008",N005:"T010",N006:"T012",N007:"T014",N008:"T016",P:"T017"},
endpoint_correspondence:{P:{mode:"direct",explanation:"The parameters are every n:ℕ (all nonnegative integers) and every set E of the Euclidean n-space GDVec n. H001 is precisely nonemptiness and H002 precisely compactness; no further project assumption is added. GDProduct E consists exactly of points (x1,…,xn,t) with x∈E and 0≤t≤1, in EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin(n+1)). Its prescribed Euclidean metric is the inherited L2 metric, with the product distance identity checked by T009. Native dimH has exactly D004's nonnegative extended-real critical-exponent definition; T001/T002 connect its measure to the given unnormalized covers. Thus the terminal equality is the whole required dim_H(E×[0,1])=dim_H(E)+1, including n=0, under exactly the original hypotheses."}}
};
