def GDInterval`);
const lineStep={id:"T018",statement:`Isometry GDLine ∧ Function.Bijective GDLine ∧
  ∀ A : Set ℝ,
    dimH (GDLine '' A) = dimH A ∧
    (∀ s δ : ℝ, 0 < s → 0 < δ →
      GDContent s δ (GDLine '' A) = GDContent s δ A) ∧
    (∀ s : ℝ, 0 < s → GDMeasure s (GDLine '' A) = GDMeasure s A)`,inputs:[],source_steps:["S007","S010"],explanation:"Checked implementation identification of the source's ℝ with its one-coordinate Euclidean space. GDLine puts t in the only coordinate and is a bijective isometry by the L2 metric formula. Transporting covers in both directions gives equality of the positive-exponent scale contents and measures. Native Hausdorff dimension is preserved by this isometry as well. This supplies the actual conversion needed to apply the m=1 instance of N001 to interval sets; no new mathematical assumption or norm comparison is introduced."};
